 {
  "n": 33,
  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 105,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1,200-1,260/month (Aug-Sep 2026, E-07), with the surge onset coinciding with manual-read route completion falling to 88% against a 95% target across 9,200 manual-read accounts in Aug-Sep (E-01). Missed manual reads trigger estimate substitution in the billing-import step of the meter-to-cash process, and estimated bills are a documented driver of disputes (1,240 of 3,025 disputed bills, 41%, are ESTIMATED-read, E-03), making the manual-read route-completion shortfall the best-evidenced contributing cause of the dispute surge among the hypotheses tested. This mechanism does not account for the ACTUAL-read majority of disputed bills (59%, E-03), which remains an open question, and ticket response times are already within the 3.0-day SLA (E-02), ruling out the requester's response-automation framing as the fix."
 },
