  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 113.0,
  "event_seq": 246,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul 2026) to ~1,180-1,260/month (Aug-Sep 2026, E-07). The surge traces to billing-import validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 with no unit scaling (E-11), which compares raw AMI register values directly against 12-month m3 consumption history; firmware v4.2 meters (rollout 2026-06) report register values in units of 0.1 m3 rather than m3 (E-12), causing BV-17 to misflag their reads as high-consumption anomalies and reject them at import as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION. This mechanism accounts for 1,184 of the 1,240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (the remaining 56 had no AMI read received at all), with billing substituting estimates for these rejected/missing reads, producing bills customers dispute (E-10). This explains the ESTIMATED-read portion (41%) of disputes but not the ACTUAL-read majority (59%, E-03), which remains open."
 },
